# gpu-nvidia: NVIDIA open kernel modules via DKMS (Blackwell / RTX 50 need the open modules).
# DKMS needs headers for every installed kernel: linux-headers matches the stock `linux` kernel,
# install the matching *-headers package yourself when running another kernel.
# The installer never touches mkinitcpio/initramfs or the kernel command line.
# lib32 packages need [multilib].
nvidia-open-dkms
nvidia-utils
nvidia-settings
dkms
linux-headers
egl-wayland
libva-nvidia-driver
lib32-nvidia-utils
